cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use noisefinder in your research, please cite the article listed under preferred-citation."
title: "noisefinder"
type: software

abstract: >-
  Noisefinder is a Python package for precise spectral estimation and noise
  decorrelation. It measures the spectral properties of time series, providing
  Bayesian confidence intervals that remain accurate when the number of
  available averaging windows is very low, for instance at very-low
  frequencies. It also performs noise projection (time series decorrelation),
  allowing for precise retrieval of background noise in the presence of
  disturbing sources.

authors:
